FAITHFUL PAPER-FIGURE EXAMPLE PROVENANCE

The paper-specific Python gallery under skills/nature-figure was reorganized
from:

  Project: figures4papers
  Repository: https://github.com/ChenLiu-1996/figures4papers
  Source revision: 6e9ca1200f4b1445cff68a42be76f7712ec2d4e1

We thank Chen Liu for making these paper-figure practices publicly available.
The skill retains 25 Python source files, 29 upstream Python-rendered PNGs,
three companion PDFs, and ten hybrid reference PNGs. They are reorganized into
`scripts/paper_examples/` and `assets/paper-patterns/` rather than copying the
source repository shell. Exact source paths, hashes, dimensions, and revision
are recorded in `assets/paper-patterns/manifest.json`.

The preserved outputs are visual golden references. Paper-specific style,
layout, drawing order, and save settings remain local to each example. Later
code refactoring is constrained by image comparison. Five selected source files
were narrowly curated with user approval; their upstream and current hashes are
both recorded, and approved derived renders remain under `optimized/` rather
than replacing upstream goldens. Unresolved scientific-policy samples remain
present and flagged for explicit review rather than silently removed.
